When the framework is not `@storybook/react-vite`, the function silently returns with no output and no error. A user running `storybook ai init` on a Vue, Angular, Svelte, or Webpack project will see nothing — no prompt, no error, no explanation of what happened. This is confusing. At minimum, emit a clear message before returning, e.g.:
```ts
logger.warn(
  `storybook ai init currently only supports @storybook/react-vite projects. Detected framework: ${projectInfo.framework}`
);
process.exit(0);
```
